From 1f66d21dedd08c5adca3f5a13913f8330c3df4ed Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alastair D'Silva <alastair@d-silva.org>
Date: Sat, 15 Aug 2026 20:21:11 +1000
Subject: [PATCH 04/29] sunxi: Add Allwinner A733 SoC support

Add baseline SoC support for the Allwinner A733 / T736 (sun60iw2) SoC.
The A733 belongs to the NCAT2 generation, featuring ARMv8 cores,
new CCU / PIO architecture, DW-based LPDDR5 memory controller,
and Synopsys DWC Ethernet QoS GMAC.

This implementation builds upon the NCAT2 SoC infrastructure introduced
for the Allwinner A523 by Andre Przywara and Jernej Skrabec, extending
it with A733-specific register base addresses, RVBAR address (0x08001004),
BL31 base, early UART0 pinmux on PB0/PB1, and DRAM controller bindings.

- Introduce CONFIG_MACH_SUN60I_A733 and CONFIG_DRAM_SUN60I_A733
- Add base register offsets in cpu_sunxi_ncat2.h
- Add UART0 pinmux definitions in sunxi_gpio.h and board.c
- Add DRAM controller build rules and timings
- Add clock initialization in clock_sun50i_h6.c

Signed-off-by: Alastair D'Silva <alastair@d-silva.org>
Assisted-by: Antigravity <antigravity@google.com>
